# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
bin/
obj/
artifacts/
publish/
TestResults/
*.binlog
*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Anything that could carry camera credentials, LAN topology, or device state
#
# The app deliberately keeps all of this under %LOCALAPPDATA%\TapoViewer and
# never inside the repo, so these patterns are defence in depth: they matter
# the moment someone copies a real config in to reproduce a bug.
#
# cameras.json holds no passwords by design (they live in Windows Credential
# Manager) but it does reveal internal addresses, ports and camera names.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
cameras.json
cameras.json.bak
cameras.json.tmp
cameras.json.*
app.log
secrets/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Key material and environment files. None exist today; these exist so an
# accidental `git add -A` after dropping a cert in the tree cannot commit it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pfx
*.snk
*.p12
*.pem
*.key
*.env
.env
.env.*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local tooling state. settings.local.json records absolute paths and the
# developer's Windows username; settings.json (shared config) is fine to commit.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/settings.local.json
*.local.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IDE and OS noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates
*.DotSettings.user
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
